# Documentation maintenance

`docs/contributions.md` is the product-manual policy. This rule covers where
implementation detail goes while the hot-server design is concentrated.

## Single technical design home

- Put all implementation detail in
  `docs/technical/architecture/low-level-design.md` (the LLD).
- Do not add new architecture pages for slices of that design (schema notes,
  process foundation, outbox shape, and similar). Update the LLD instead.
- Split a topic out of the LLD only when the team explicitly asks for a later
  split.

## What other docs may hold

- `docs/technical/architecture/local-development.md`: This is running memory/ scratch pad. This will never be commited. Make all implementation updates in the LLD.
- `docs/technical/architecture/high-level-design.md`: product-level shape, not
  table-level or process-level or implementation detail.
- `docs/functional/`: observable product behavior only, once it exists.
- Issues hold acceptance criteria. Do not copy those into the manual.

